 { This position is taken from a game of mine, Al-Modiakhi,M - Astaneh Lopez,A (2008) . I'm in some trouble here owing to my damaged structure. Can you find the strong move that my Grandmaster opponent played? } 17. { -KEY- } Bc5 $1 { A nasty move! White spots that Black's pawns are mostly placed on light squares. To exploit this, he forces a trade of the dark-squared bishops. } Bf6 18. Bxf8 Bxa1 19. Rxa1 Kxf8 20. Rd1 { The rook re-establishes itself on the open file. } Ke7 ( 20... f4 $1 { Shifting my pawn to a dark square was my best bet, in order to breathe some life into my light-squared bishop. } ) 
